{"id":"3a6ab09b3579e778","group":"58","path":"58/batch04/58-df-height-function.md","title":"Height Function","display":"df-height-function — Height Function","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-height-function","aliases":["58-df-height-function"],"display":"df-height-function — Height Function","depends_on":["[[../batch19/58-df-projective-space.md]]","[[../batch10/58-df-elliptic-curve.md]]","[[../batch12/58-df-field-extension.md]]","[[../batch16/58-df-function.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-height-function"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-height-function</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-height-function — Height Function"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"24c725a359792259\" href=\"?note=24c725a359792259\" title=\"../batch19/58-df-projective-space.md\">../batch19/58-df-projective-space.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"74f4744df7db749f\" href=\"?note=74f4744df7db749f\" title=\"../batch10/58-df-elliptic-curve.md\">../batch10/58-df-elliptic-curve.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"699918fd54cc2a8e\" href=\"?note=699918fd54cc2a8e\" title=\"../batch12/58-df-field-extension.md\">../batch12/58-df-field-extension.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"36d7463d215be751\" href=\"?note=36d7463d215be751\" title=\"../batch16/58-df-function.md\">../batch16/58-df-function.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"K,N,M_K,w,\\operatorname{abs},h,H\\in V\">\\(K,N,M_K,w,\\operatorname{abs},h,H\\in V\\)</span> (number field, dimension, places, local weights and absolute values, logarithmic and multiplicative heights)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{FieldExtension}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{FieldExtension}_S\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Function}\">\\(\\mathrm{Function}\\)</span> are predicates from dependencies.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{WeilHeightStructure}_S\\subseteq V^7\">\\(\\mathrm{WeilHeightStructure}_S\\subseteq V^7\\)</span> (predicate defined here)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}height\\text{-}function} \\vdash \\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{WeilHeightStructure}_S(h,H,K,N,M_K,w,\\operatorname{abs})\\leftrightarrow{}&amp;\\mathrm{FieldExtension}_S(K,\\mathbb Q)\\land[K:\\mathbb Q]&lt;\\aleph_0\\land N\\in\\omega\\\\\n&amp;{}\\land\\mathrm{Function}(w,M_K,\\mathbb R_{&gt;0})\\land\\mathrm{Function}(\\operatorname{abs},M_K,\\operatorname{ran}(\\operatorname{abs}))\\\\\n&amp;{}\\land\\forall v\\in M_K\\;\\mathrm{Function}(\\operatorname{abs}(v),K,\\mathbb R_{\\geq0})\\\\\n&amp;{}\\land\\mathrm{Function}(h,\\mathbb P^N(K),\\mathbb R)\\land\\mathrm{Function}(H,\\mathbb P^N(K),\\mathbb R_{&gt;0})\\\\\n&amp;{}\\land\\forall(x_0,\\ldots,x_N)\\in K^{N+1}\\setminus\\{0\\}\\;\\left(h([x_0:\\cdots:x_N])=\\frac1{[K:\\mathbb Q]}\\sum_{v\\in M_K}w(v)\\log\\max_{i\\leq N}\\operatorname{abs}(v)(x_i)\\right)\\\\\n&amp;{}\\land\\forall x\\in\\mathbb P^N(K)\\;(H(x)=\\exp(h(x))).\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}height\\text{-}function} \\vdash \\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{WeilHeightStructure}_S(h,H,K,N,M_K,w,\\operatorname{abs})\\leftrightarrow{}&amp;\\mathrm{FieldExtension}_S(K,\\mathbb Q)\\land[K:\\mathbb Q]&lt;\\aleph_0\\land N\\in\\omega\\\\\n&amp;{}\\land\\mathrm{Function}(w,M_K,\\mathbb R_{&gt;0})\\land\\mathrm{Function}(\\operatorname{abs},M_K,\\operatorname{ran}(\\operatorname{abs}))\\\\\n&amp;{}\\land\\forall v\\in M_K\\;\\mathrm{Function}(\\operatorname{abs}(v),K,\\mathbb R_{\\geq0})\\\\\n&amp;{}\\land\\mathrm{Function}(h,\\mathbb P^N(K),\\mathbb R)\\land\\mathrm{Function}(H,\\mathbb P^N(K),\\mathbb R_{&gt;0})\\\\\n&amp;{}\\land\\forall(x_0,\\ldots,x_N)\\in K^{N+1}\\setminus\\{0\\}\\;\\left(h([x_0:\\cdots:x_N])=\\frac1{[K:\\mathbb Q]}\\sum_{v\\in M_K}w(v)\\log\\max_{i\\leq N}\\operatorname{abs}(v)(x_i)\\right)\\\\\n&amp;{}\\land\\forall x\\in\\mathbb P^N(K)\\;(H(x)=\\exp(h(x))).\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The local place set, weights, normalized absolute values, dimension, and both height maps are explicit data; independence of homogeneous coordinates follows from the product formula and is a downstream theorem.</li>\n<li>Canonical height <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\hat{h}\">\\(\\hat{h}\\)</span> is quadratic on elliptic curves.</li>\n<li>Néron–Tate height on abelian varieties.</li>\n<li>Northcott's theorem: finitely many points of bounded height.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch19/58-df-projective-space.md","status":"resolved","id":"24c725a359792259","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch19/58-df-projective-space.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch10/58-df-elliptic-curve.md","status":"resolved","id":"74f4744df7db749f","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch10/58-df-elliptic-curve.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch12/58-df-field-extension.md","status":"resolved","id":"699918fd54cc2a8e","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch12/58-df-field-extension.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch16/58-df-function.md","status":"resolved","id":"36d7463d215be751","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch16/58-df-function.md]]","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"K,N,M_K,w,\\operatorname{abs},h,H\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{FieldExtension}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Function}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{WeilHeightStructure}_S\\subseteq V^7","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}height\\text{-}function} \\vdash \\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{WeilHeightStructure}_S(h,H,K,N,M_K,w,\\operatorname{abs})\\leftrightarrow{}&\\mathrm{FieldExtension}_S(K,\\mathbb Q)\\land[K:\\mathbb Q]<\\aleph_0\\land N\\in\\omega\\\\\n&{}\\land\\mathrm{Function}(w,M_K,\\mathbb R_{>0})\\land\\mathrm{Function}(\\operatorname{abs},M_K,\\operatorname{ran}(\\operatorname{abs}))\\\\\n&{}\\land\\forall v\\in M_K\\;\\mathrm{Function}(\\operatorname{abs}(v),K,\\mathbb R_{\\geq0})\\\\\n&{}\\land\\mathrm{Function}(h,\\mathbb P^N(K),\\mathbb R)\\land\\mathrm{Function}(H,\\mathbb P^N(K),\\mathbb R_{>0})\\\\\n&{}\\land\\forall(x_0,\\ldots,x_N)\\in K^{N+1}\\setminus\\{0\\}\\;\\left(h([x_0:\\cdots:x_N])=\\frac1{[K:\\mathbb Q]}\\sum_{v\\in M_K}w(v)\\log\\max_{i\\leq N}\\operatorname{abs}(v)(x_i)\\right)\\\\\n&{}\\land\\forall x\\in\\mathbb P^N(K)\\;(H(x)=\\exp(h(x))).\n\\end{aligned}","display":true},{"tex":"\\hat{h}","display":false}],"bytes":1986,"backlinks":[{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-614","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch04/58-df-height-function.md|58-df-height-function]]（batch04）"}],"outgoing":["24c725a359792259","74f4744df7db749f","699918fd54cc2a8e","36d7463d215be751"]}